# Precompile statements for the application bundle. GENERATED — do not edit by hand.
#
# `bin/trace.jl` is the execution trace and, unlike OITOOLS', it OPENS THE WINDOW: `gui()`
# takes `autoquit_ms`, so `loadqml`, the QML engine and the first frame are already in the
# image from it. What a statements file adds on top is the paths one run cannot reach — the
# other tabs, the fit engines, the file picker — and the specialisations a real session
# provokes that a scripted one does not.
#
# Regenerate by unioning traces:
#
#     xvfb-run -a julia --project=bin --trace-compile=a.trace bin/trace.jl
#     xvfb-run -a julia --project=bin --trace-compile=b.trace test/gui/runtests.jl
#     cat *.trace | sort -u | grep -vE '\b(Main|Test)\.' > app/precompile_statements.jl
#
# The `Main.`/`Test.` filter drops the harness's own specialisations, which have no business in
# an application. PackageCompiler is tolerant of the rest: it parses each line, skips what will
# not parse, resolves an `UndefVarError` by importing the module named, and skips what it still
# cannot resolve — so a raw trace is safe to feed.
#
# COST: every statement here is compiled INTO the image, so this trades bundle size for
# first-action latency. Regenerate and re-measure rather than assuming the trade still holds.
